{"strategies":[{"id":"S1","name":"Topic favourite (momentum)","family":"Directional","side":"YES","rule":"Inside each topic, buy YES on the market with the highest 24h traded notional when its YES ask is between $0.02 and $0.98.","why":"Tests whether the money in the demo book is on the eventual winner.","select":"top_notional","order":-1,"min_price":"0.02","max_price":"0.98"},{"id":"S2","name":"Topic underdog (contrarian)","family":"Directional","side":"YES","rule":"Inside each topic, buy YES on the lowest-priced market whose YES ask is >= $0.02 and whose 24h traded notional is >= $100.","why":"Long-shot bias test: cheap YES contracts often overprice tails.","select":"cheapest_yes","order":1,"min_price":"0.02","max_price":"0.50","min_notional":"100"},{"id":"S3","name":"YES/NO pair arbitrage","family":"Relative value","side":"PAIR","rule":"Buy 1 YES and 1 NO in the same market when YES ask + NO ask < $1.00 by at least $0.01 after taker fees on both legs.","why":"A $1.00 guaranteed pair bought below $1.00 is a riskless edge if both legs fill.","select":"pair_edge","min_edge":"0.01"},{"id":"S4","name":"Heavy favourite (hold YES)","family":"Relative value","side":"YES","rule":"Buy YES where the YES ask is between $0.80 and $0.95 and the implied spread (YES ask + NO ask - $1.00) is at most $0.02, i.e. the book agrees with the favourite and the round trip is cheap.","why":"Favourite-longshot bias: heavily favoured contracts historically win slightly more often than their price implies. Tested here on demo prices.","select":"heavy_favourite","min_yes":"0.80","max_yes":"0.95","max_spread":"0.02"},{"id":"S5","name":"Wide-spread fade","family":"Liquidity","side":"NO","rule":"Buy NO where the implied spread (YES ask + NO ask - $1.00) >= $0.05 and the NO ask is between $0.02 and $0.98, i.e. the book is wide enough to justify taking the safer side.","why":"Wide books on the demo venue mean the quoted price is not a fair estimate.","select":"wide_spread","min_spread":"0.05"},{"i